From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:38:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] hbbs: forward a controller's ICE candidates only after
 its punch hole

An IceCandidate with an id went to that peer from any connection, without
a key or a ticket: anyone could push candidates at every registered PC,
each one up to the message bound and queued on the PC's signaling
connection. A controller trickles on the connection of its punch hole
request, addressed to the peer it asked for (client.rs,
spawn_webrtc_ice_bridge, which never reconnects that socket). So hbbs
now notes on each connection the peer its last punch hole request
reached, after the key, minimum version and access ticket checks, and
forwards a candidate with an id only to that peer from that connection;
others are dropped, with a debug line, and the connection stays. In
enforce mode that is a controller with an admitted ticket.

The other direction stays as it was: the PC trickles to the controller
on a connection of its own (rendezvous_mediator, one per WebRTC
session) that carries no id, so hbbs cannot tell its sender without a
change of the protocol. Such a candidate reaches only a connection that
asked for a punch hole or a relay, and the controller drops candidates
whose session_key is not its session's.

Tests: tests/untrusted_input.rs, candidates from a connection without a
punch hole request, from one whose request had the wrong key, and to
another peer are dropped, while the controller's reach its peer;
tests/access.rs, in enforce mode, from a connection whose request had no
good ticket they are dropped, from one with a staff ticket they arrive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
